namespace Death {
//###==##====#=====--==~--~=~- --- -- -  -  -   -

/** @page paths File locations
@brief Where the game reads its files from and where it writes them, on every supported platform

@tableofcontents

@section paths-overview Overview

Every platform uses the same set of directories and files, only their locations differ:

Name | What it holds | Written by the game
---- | ------------- | -------------------
@cpp "Content/" @ce | The game's own assets --- sprites, shaders, fonts, translations, bundled episodes | No
User @cpp "Content/" @ce | Your own or modded content, see @ref paths-user-content | No
@cpp "Source/" @ce | Original <em>Jazz Jackrabbit 2</em> files you copy there --- @cpp "Anims.j2a" @ce, levels, tilesets, music | No
@cpp "Cache/" @ce | @cpp "Source/" @ce files converted on the first start, the shader cache and assets downloaded from multiplayer servers. Safe to delete, it's rebuilt on the next start | Yes
@cpp "Jazz2.config" @ce | Settings and episode progress | Yes
@cpp "Jazz2.resume" @ce | Saved state for continuing an interrupted level, next to @cpp "Jazz2.config" @ce | Yes
@cpp "Jazz2.log" @ce | Log of the current session, earlier sessions are kept in @cpp "Jazz2.log.gz" @ce next to it | Yes

@m_class{m-noindent}

Below, the <b>config directory</b> means the directory with @cpp "Jazz2.config" @ce, the resume file and the log
always sit there together @m_span{m-text m-dim} (only iOS keeps the log elsewhere) @m_endspan. A
@cpp "gamecontrollerdb.txt" @ce with extra gamepad mappings is read from there and from @cpp "Content/" @ce on
most platforms. A log file is only written by builds with tracing enabled @m_span{m-text m-dim} (`DEATH_TRACE`) @m_endspan.

@subsection paths-user-content User Content directory

On platforms where @cpp "Content/" @ce is packed inside the application @m_span{m-text m-dim} (APK, app bundle,
AppImage, system-wide package, UWP package, @cpp ".nro" @ce, @cpp ".vpk" @ce) @m_endspan nothing can be added to
it, so the game also reads a second @cpp "Content/" @ce directory the user can reach --- usually next to
@cpp "Cache/" @ce. It's only used if it already exists when the game starts. Files are searched in this order:

1.  User @cpp "Content/" @ce --- a file here replaces the file with the same path anywhere below
2.  @cpp "Content/" @ce
3.  @cpp "Cache/" @ce

@m_class{m-noindent}

Translations are the exception: their order is user @cpp "Content/" @ce, @cpp "Cache/" @ce, @cpp "Content/" @ce.
While connected to a multiplayer server, the level, its tilesets and music downloaded from the server take
precedence over all of the above.

@section paths-desktop Desktop

@subsection paths-windows Windows

What | Location
---- | --------
@cpp "Content" @ce, @cpp "Source" @ce, @cpp "Cache" @ce | Next to @cpp "Jazz2.exe" @ce
Config directory | @cpp "C:\Users\<user>\Saved Games\Jazz² Resurrection" @ce @m_span{m-text m-dim} (or @cpp "AppData\Roaming\Jazz² Resurrection" @ce if there is no <em>Saved Games</em> folder) @m_endspan, or next to @cpp "Jazz2.exe" @ce if a @cpp "Jazz2.config" @ce already exists there @m_span{m-text m-dim} (portable mode) @m_endspan
Log | Only with `/log:file`, `/log` opens a console window instead

@subsection paths-linux Linux

What | Location
---- | --------
Portable @m_span{m-text m-dim} (@cpp "Content/" @ce next to the executable) @m_endspan | @cpp "Content/" @ce, @cpp "Source/" @ce and @cpp "Cache/" @ce next to the executable
Installed package @m_span{m-text m-dim} (DEB, RPM, distribution packages) @m_endspan | @cpp "Content/" @ce in @cpp "/usr/share/jazz2/" @ce @m_span{m-text m-dim} (install prefix and package name) @m_endspan, @cpp "Source/" @ce and @cpp "Cache/" @ce in @cpp "~/.local/share/jazz2/" @ce @m_span{m-text m-dim} (`$XDG_DATA_HOME`; @cpp "~/.local/share/Jazz² Resurrection/" @ce is used instead if it has a @cpp "Cache/" @ce) @m_endspan. A @cpp "Source/" @ce in @cpp "/usr/share/jazz2/" @ce is used if the per-user one doesn't contain the game files
AppImage | @cpp "Content/" @ce inside the image, @cpp "Source/" @ce and @cpp "Cache/" @ce next to the @cpp ".AppImage" @ce file if @cpp "Source/" @ce there contains the game files, otherwise in @cpp "~/.local/share/jazz2/" @ce
Flatpak | @cpp "Content/" @ce in @cpp "/app/share/Jazz² Resurrection/" @ce, everything else under @cpp "~/.var/app/dev.de4th.jazz2/" @ce
User @cpp "Content/" @ce | Next to @cpp "Cache/" @ce, if it isn't the same as @cpp "Content/" @ce
Config directory | @cpp "~/.config/Jazz² Resurrection/" @ce @m_span{m-text m-dim} (`$XDG_CONFIG_HOME`; @cpp "~/.config/jazz2/" @ce for AppImage) @m_endspan, or the working directory if a @cpp "Jazz2.config" @ce already exists there
Log | Only with `/log:file`

@subsection paths-macos macOS

What | Location
---- | --------
@cpp "Content/" @ce | Inside the application bundle
@cpp "Source/" @ce, @cpp "Cache/" @ce, user @cpp "Content/" @ce | @cpp "~/Library/Application Support/Jazz² Resurrection/" @ce
Config directory | @cpp "~/Library/Application Support/Jazz² Resurrection/" @ce, or the working directory if a @cpp "Jazz2.config" @ce already exists there
Log | Only with `/log:file`

@subsection paths-cmdline Command-line options

These work on Windows, Linux and macOS:

-   `/config <path>` --- use this configuration file, its directory becomes the config directory
-   `/reset-config` --- start with the default settings
-   `/log:file` --- write @cpp "Jazz2.log" @ce into the config directory, `/log:file:<name>` uses another name
    @m_span{m-text m-dim} (relative to the config directory, the earlier sessions aren't archived then) @m_endspan
-   `/log` --- Windows only, opens a console window with the log

@m_class{m-noindent}

A build configured with `DEATH_TRACE_LOG_PATH` always writes the log under that name into the config directory.

@section paths-mobile Mobile

@subsection paths-android Android

What | Location
---- | --------
@cpp "Content/" @ce | Inside the APK
@cpp "Source/" @ce, @cpp "Cache/" @ce, user @cpp "Content/" @ce | With <em>All files access</em> granted: the first existing of @cpp "Games/Jazz² Resurrection/" @ce, @cpp "Games/Jazz2 Resurrection/" @ce, @cpp "Download/Jazz² Resurrection/" @ce and @cpp "Download/Jazz2 Resurrection/" @ce on the internal storage, @cpp "Games/Jazz² Resurrection/" @ce if none exists. Otherwise @cpp "Android/data/jazz2.resurrection/files/" @ce
Config directory | Next to @cpp "Source/" @ce @m_span{m-text m-dim} (a @cpp "Jazz2.config" @ce from older versions in the app's private storage is kept until one exists next to @cpp "Source/" @ce) @m_endspan
Log | @cpp "Jazz2.log" @ce in the config directory, always

@subsection paths-ios iOS

What | Location
---- | --------
@cpp "Content/" @ce | Inside the application bundle
@cpp "Source/" @ce, user @cpp "Content/" @ce | The app's @cpp "Documents/" @ce folder, visible in the <em>Files</em> app
@cpp "Cache/" @ce | @cpp "Library/Caches/" @ce @m_span{m-text m-dim} (not visible, may be purged by the system) @m_endspan
Config directory | @cpp "Library/Application Support/Jazz² Resurrection/" @ce
Log | @cpp "Documents/Jazz2.log" @ce, always

@section paths-other Other platforms

@subsection paths-uwp Windows RT (UWP, Xbox)

What | Location
---- | --------
@cpp "Content" @ce | Inside the application package
@cpp "Source" @ce, @cpp "Cache" @ce, user @cpp "Content" @ce | On Xbox the first of @cpp "D:" @ce to @cpp "G:" @ce drives with @cpp "Games\Jazz² Resurrection\Source" @ce @m_span{m-text m-dim} (or @cpp "Jazz2 Resurrection" @ce) @m_endspan, otherwise the app's @cpp "LocalState" @ce folder
Config directory | Next to @cpp "Source" @ce if writable, otherwise @cpp "LocalState" @ce
Log | None

@subsection paths-web Web (Emscripten)

Everything lives in the browser. @cpp "Content/" @ce is preloaded with the page, the config directory is
@cpp "/Persistent/" @ce @m_span{m-text m-dim} (stored in the browser's IndexedDB) @m_endspan, and the log only
goes to the browser console.

@subsection paths-libretro Libretro core

@cpp "Content/" @ce, @cpp "Source/" @ce and @cpp "Cache/" @ce are looked up in the frontend's <em>system</em>
directory @m_span{m-text m-dim} (directly or in its @cpp "jazz2/" @ce subdirectory) @m_endspan, the config
directory is @cpp "jazz2/" @ce in the frontend's <em>save</em> directory.

@subsection paths-amiga Amiga

Everything --- @cpp "Content/" @ce, @cpp "Source/" @ce, @cpp "Cache/" @ce and @cpp "Jazz2.config" @ce --- sits
in the game's own directory. No log file is written.

@subsection paths-server Dedicated server

Uses the same directories as the game on the same platform. Its configuration is
@cpp "Jazz2.Server.config" @ce in the working directory, or the path given after `/server`, see
@ref multiplayer-config.

@section paths-consoles Consoles

The config directory is next to @cpp "Source/" @ce, and @cpp "Jazz2.log" @ce is written there, unless stated
otherwise. See also @ref consoles for how each build is packaged.

Console | Content directory | Source, cache and config directory | Notes
------- | ----------------- | ---------------------------------- | -----
Nintendo Switch | @cpp "romfs:/" @ce @m_span{m-text m-dim} (inside the @cpp ".nro" @ce) @m_endspan | @cpp "sdmc:/Games/Jazz2/" @ce | User @cpp "Content/" @ce in @cpp "sdmc:/Games/Jazz2/Content/" @ce
Nintendo 3DS | @cpp "sdmc:/3ds/Jazz2/Content/" @ce | @cpp "sdmc:/3ds/Jazz2/" @ce | ---
Nintendo Wii | @cpp "sd:/apps/Jazz2/Content/" @ce | @cpp "sd:/apps/Jazz2/" @ce | ---
Nintendo GameCube | @cpp "Jazz2/Content/" @ce on an SD card, or @cpp "dvd:/Content/" @ce | Next to @cpp "Content/" @ce | From the disc, @cpp "Jazz2.config" @ce and @cpp "Jazz2.resume" @ce go to a memory card @m_span{m-text m-dim} (@cpp "mca:/" @ce, or @cpp "mcb:/" @ce) @m_endspan and no log is written
Nintendo 64 | @cpp "rom:/Content/" @ce | @cpp "rom:/Cache/" @ce, read-only | Settings go to the cartridge EEPROM @m_span{m-text m-dim} (@cpp "eeprom:/JAZZ2CFG" @ce) @m_endspan, no resume file and no log
PlayStation Vita | @cpp "app0:/Content/" @ce @m_span{m-text m-dim} (inside the VPK) @m_endspan | @cpp "ux0:/data/jazz2/" @ce | User @cpp "Content/" @ce in @cpp "ux0:/data/jazz2/Content/" @ce
PlayStation Portable | @cpp "ms0:/PSP/GAME/Jazz2/Content/" @ce | @cpp "ms0:/PSP/GAME/Jazz2/" @ce | ---
PlayStation 3 | @cpp "/app_home/Content/" @ce @m_span{m-text m-dim} (next to @cpp "EBOOT.BIN" @ce) @m_endspan | @cpp "Source/" @ce in @cpp "/app_home/" @ce, @cpp "Cache/" @ce in @cpp "/dev_hdd0/game/<APPID>/USRDIR/" @ce | @cpp "Jazz2.config" @ce in the working directory, no log
PlayStation 2 | @cpp "Content/" @ce next to the executable, in @cpp "Games/Jazz2/" @ce on a USB stick or MX4SIO SD card, or @cpp "cdfs:/Content/" @ce | Next to @cpp "Content/" @ce | From the disc, @cpp "Jazz2.config" @ce goes to a memory card @m_span{m-text m-dim} (@cpp "mc0:/Jazz2/" @ce, or @cpp "mc1:/Jazz2/" @ce) @m_endspan and no log is written
Sega Dreamcast | @cpp "/cd/Content/" @ce | @cpp "/cd/" @ce, read-only | @cpp "Jazz2.config" @ce and @cpp "Jazz2.resume" @ce go to the first VMU @m_span{m-text m-dim} (@cpp "/vmu/a1/Jazz2" @ce for port A, unit 1) @m_endspan, no log

*/

}
